{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as a design-adoption input: complete R0 contract at exact e6ae8010061924a52afb5b506193c54e5b3de425, under current request ed7f5b00534f045425318c07b07bf0f98aca0c61, builder promise 5c0e08d3dd30275cd8753f1879b5679e774e8829, invitation b5c46c6eca6d2ad9cf3e04fa62b1d325a3c73299 and checker promise 65248042ede97050edeb63241a71db7b2089f4d1. Primary 5a52dc86 comes first and all seven current artifacts are included. No blocking finding remains in this R0 scope. This is a new independent evidence-only assessment on live bases, not revival of historical approval 92abd211 or ratification 990422cf. It is not mergeable and closes no source implementation.\n\nArchitecture. The complete fifteen-step issue-to-contribution-to-exact-result journey preserves separate commitments, blocking interface requests, agreed handover, exact versions, failed combined checks, independent review/revision, changed destination base, lost publication reply and confirmed result. The thirty browser outcomes and compact fault variants retain leave-A/return-B/watch/steer/review, private-state and checkpoint recovery duties. Responsibility, temporary holds, agent execution, selected contribution facts, review subjects and publication results remain distinct. Local admission, causal receipts, source-owned relationship delivery and unrelated-lane progress are acceptance requirements, not measured scalability. R1 owns precise language/replay, R2 forms and dated parity, R3 authority/effects, R4 proof/cost. This verdict adopts none of those drafts.\n\nSecurity. The design preserves grant/key/member boundaries, observed authority windows, authorized private handover/export, last-owner-key-loss quiescence, checkpoint payload and object closure, guarded receipts/current pointers, epoch plus execution-instance fences and stale-callback refusal. Missing storage cannot silently become an empty replacement. Observed exit remains distinct from a durable result. Publication unknowns retain all attempts and writing credentials until fenced, drained or reconciled; the old branch tip alone cannot settle an earlier send. Pins, tombstones and owned retry protect deletion. E1 must separately list live resources, retain unresolved outside duties with owners, and settle/account for them before authorized reset/removal. Historical configurations, inventories and notes establish no current absence.\n\nSimplification. Every listed package/module category/export/bin/test set/runner/script/configuration/storage group/agent runtime/spike/guide/example/manual component and named sibling application has a successor or explicit retirement scope. Removal belongs to each replacement; I8 audits the resulting single model. Jam must run on the chosen composition or have no active old runtime. Release outputs and linked checkouts are derived material, with clean-state/recoverable-head/owner checks before removal. No legacy wire adapter, dual engine, old identity mapping or prior-format replay is required. Retained code and invariants must earn a new-model role. Test economy preserves the useful 10x goal and install-to-review cost accounting, removes obsolete suites, and uses compact invariant and real-boundary witnesses. No narrow successful demo or estimate replaces full acceptance.\n\nObligations and limits. The seventy-row dated ledger is a reconciliation proposal, not a closure act. Each party must freshly read and personally reconcile its current commitments. Old request IDs are historical snapshot anchors; current commissioning must bind their live successors. Request-ready I1–I8/IA/E1 scopes remain contingent on separately adopted interfaces/designs. C2 keeps both isolated-storage/process and integrated authority/custody/fencing delivery boundaries. Joint 017/018 adoption, R1–R4 decisions, live settlement, source acceptance, application parity, measured capacity and the deployed walkthrough remain separate work. The expanded R3v7/R2v10 contracts and the exact-foreign-start P2 in checker assessment da88fb08 are outside this R0 verdict; no full-project approval is implied.\n\nFresh evidence. Exact head is the direct child of a3d0ce4c5337c98bf1e9f507813d3b8605c03894 and changes only the new 22-line refile note. Root independently verified every current SHA256 and Git blob and confirmed all six original files are byte-identical to the earlier fully read files. The whole new note and complete diff were read. Previous complete six-file and frozen 017/018 reads and independent source/70-row census checks are reused only as immutable reading evidence. Root cross-read current external-duty, test-economy, commissioning and acceptance sections; a separate static reader confirmed full original request text is the replacement's exact prefix, with identical conditions, and checked refile/governance and scope sections. All seven current artifact records were inspected: exact same head, each directly under live builder promise 5c0e08d3. Ordinary prepare confirms evidence-only binding to ed7f5b00. The registered detached checkout /tmp/artroom-checker-r0-e6ae8010-qYVSY8/checkout is clean at the exact candidate; every checkout document SHA matches its frozen Git bytes.\n\nRead/identity ledger: main 118495 bytes/1300 lines, SHA256 9b66892b2a865319f96ebf1f4681e7ec6b271253d3970c65b38ab054a1cc1dbf, blob 953edea93c2256a6f915ea90099bffb3d23ba6cc; corrections 8215/40, SHA256 7bf04a5c0088ecb830d2dce1899ecfcb92f468f4d95fd64f3e0082f208b83967, blob 3b72faaed93a060699c08285c1c53fc0512909f7; ledger-source 10546/76, SHA256 950019ed99a0d920977d9891447f6c7095f829cbc68cdcf4b712d93617cd054b, blob 71012a33858dbc7ede2bdc063087f22c7ed36f09; source inventory 73682/785, SHA256 71b913b5440659a639503132797d152de14676246c812d0a8e40495d061437b8, blob 8d3e13e9667a202f88d4d4fbabd4b4639149b39a; workroom inventory 66516/293, SHA256 ad0c8c0335d8d1bbfb5589703ed9ce347c48d1ec03e2377127e9f6f4ba4b2d8f, blob d8026c4521572d291bfa299a26e351c42d31b881; documents/repositories inventory 51292/442, SHA256 8f5c86141f75d2b4eb9edfefde79f71ed54d2bb18ede50e39119a4296ad46efb, blob 5923c42bf49ac82b009ed9bb0178433b597b675b; refile 1244/22, SHA256 e745747cd3af5d00cd98ac610c82781ef201b5f9fcefc8229d7c78ee6afc8630, blob 83e3f6f946635a6428c7271bd71fd031138b6e3d.\n\nNonblocking erratum. Main 941 names three measurement configuration files while saying four. Refile 16–19 expressly applies the content of historical erratum 2abe4923, leaving I4 retirement unchanged. That incorporation does not revive the stale erratum's causal force. Section 13's unavailable-reviewer statement records preparation-time history; the standing checker is active and this new review resolves only the present R0 invitation. The dated inventories do not claim coverage of later work or semantic source safety. GitHub parity and host safe-repeat proofs remain separately owed.\n\nOnly static source/document/provenance reads and normal review lifecycle actions were performed. No repository/package execution, tests, install, build, probe, private diagnostic, provider read, source edit, merge, deployment or outside-person message occurred. The retired private diagnostic was neither rerun nor delegated. Approval permits R0 design adoption through the requester's proper act; it supplies no implementation or deletion authority.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5a52dc86f0c5e41b706ef80b067213fdf1235d39","binding":"evidence-only","head":"e6ae8010061924a52afb5b506193c54e5b3de425","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65248042ede97050edeb63241a71db7b2089f4d1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f061d618cfeb1bc3237bff542b5fe84b5d618638","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}